diff --git a/SLURM_DDP_HANG_HANDOFF.md b/SLURM_DDP_HANG_HANDOFF.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1234567
--- /dev/null
+++ b/SLURM_DDP_HANG_HANDOFF.md
@@ -0,0 +1,106 @@
+# SLURM/submitit multi-GPU DDP "hang" — RESOLVED
+
+**Status (2026-07-15, updated):** ROOT-CAUSED. It was never an NCCL collective
+desync, a launcher bug, `optimize_ddp`, or the compile warmup. **It is a rank-0
+CUDA OutOfMemoryError, masked by a barrier so it looked like a collective hang.**
+
+## The actual root cause
+On the failing 8-GPU runs, rank 0 OOMs during the first backbone forward (Liger
+`FusedLinearCrossEntropy`), then unwinds into `reproducibility.__exit__`'s
+`barrier()`, which blocks forever (peers are still training / cold-compiling and
+never arrive) and SWALLOWS the traceback. NCCL then reports a downstream
+collective-count/size mismatch on the healthy ranks 30 min later — which is the
+"rank-0-conditional numel=1-vs-147 desync" this doc previously chased. That
+mismatch was a *symptom* of rank 0 dying mid-step, not the cause.
+
+Unmasked traceback (captured after adding logging to the warmup):
+```
+torch.OutOfMemoryError: CUDA out of memory. Tried to allocate 198.00 MiB.
+GPU 0 has a total capacity of 79.44 GiB of which 169.62 MiB is free.
+this process has 65.38 GiB memory in use. Process <PID> has 13.88 GiB memory in use.
+  ... liger_kernel/ops/fused_linear_cross_entropy.py:134
+      grad_weight += torch.mm(grad_logits_chunk.t(), _input_chunk).float()
+```
+
+**The co-tenant that OOM'd rank 0 = a foreign process holding ~13.88 GiB on the
+training node's GPU 0.** Two contributing factors, now understood:
+
+1. **PRIMARY TRIGGER (fixed by the user 2026-07-15):** the user's `radeval_service`
+   (uvicorn VLM-eval server) had a bug where it **auto-started on SSH into a node**.
+   So when a training job landed on a compute node — or when anyone ssh'd in to
+   inspect it — radeval spawned and grabbed ~14 GiB on GPU 0. This is why the OOM
+   looked random/rank-0-conditional/node-dependent, and why the user (who didn't
+   trigger the autostart) only ever saw radeval on its intended dev node GPU-658.
+   The autostart bug is now fixed (verified: ssh into a fresh compute node no
+   longer spawns radeval). radeval is a per-node systemd --user unit for dev nodes
+   (GPU-658/670) ONLY — it does not legitimately run on SLURM compute nodes.
+
+   [Correction note: an earlier version of this doc claimed a persistent radeval
+   instance was deployed on GPU-88. That was a misattribution — post-cancellation
+   `ps -p <pid>` lookups on recycled PIDs. The real mechanism was autostart-on-ssh.]
+
+2. **GENERAL VULNERABILITY (still present):** this cluster shares nodes across users
+   — `scontrol show partition compute` → `ExclusiveUser=NO`, and `launch_slurm.py`
+   requests `--nodelist` but NOT `--exclusive`. So any other tenant's process on
+   rank 0's GPU (e.g. `dawei_gu`'s 8-GPU jobs currently on GPU-88/142/229) can
+   OOM rank 0 the same way. Fixing radeval removes the main trigger but not the
+   class.
+
+Rank 0 (already ~65 GiB at 1024d/24L/32k-ctx, activation_checkpointing:false) has
+almost no headroom, so any co-tenant on its GPU tips it into OOM while clean ranks
+1-7 (~68 GiB, alone on their GPUs) survive → the asymmetry. torchrun on GPU-670
+"worked" only because that node's GPU 0 was clean at the time.
+
+**Status / actions:** radeval autostart-on-ssh is fixed. For robustness against
+generic GPU sharing, either request `--exclusive` node allocation in launch_slurm
+OR preflight-check GPU 0 is empty before launch, and/or set
+`activation_checkpointing: true` for headroom. Once rank 0's GPU is clean the
+config trains (the 4-GPU smokes that passed all landed on clean-GPU-0 nodes).
+
+## ACTION FOR THE SWEEP AGENT (you)
+1. **Do not launch training onto nodes whose GPU 0 already has foreign memory.**
+   Before/at submit, check `nvidia-smi --query-compute-apps` on the target node,
+   or prefer nodes SLURM reports idle AND verify GPU 0 is empty. (Under a proper
+   SLURM allocation with exclusive node access this won't happen — the issue is
+   the radeval service ignoring SLURM.)
+2. **Keep `radeval_service` OFF the compute pool.** It's meant to live on GPU-658
+   (a SLURM-`down` node per its own deploy.sh comment). Confirm its
+   systemd `run_service.sh` GPU-selection is pinned to GPU-658, not "first free
+   GPU on whatever node it's invoked on." Right now a green/blue instance is
+   squatting compute nodes (GPU-88/142) and colliding with training.
+3. Config note: 1024d/24L/32k-ctx/`activation_checkpointing:false` puts rank 0 at
+   ~65 GiB even clean — very little headroom. If you want robustness to any
+   co-tenant or a future larger model, enable `activation_checkpointing: true`
+   (~20-30% slower, big memory win) or lower per-rank load. Not required once
+   GPU 0 is clean, but the run is one stray process away from OOM as-is.
+
+## Fixes already landed (make the failure LOUD instead of a silent hang)
+- `tunalab reproducibility.py::__exit__` — the cleanup `barrier()` now runs ONLY
+  on a clean exit (`exc_type is None`). On an exception exit it is skipped so the
+  failing rank finishes unwinding and PRINTS ITS TRACEBACK instead of deadlocking
+  the job. Kills the whole "masked single-rank error → fake DDP hang" class.
+  Test: `tests/src/tunalab/test_reproducibility.py::test_exit_barrier_skipped_on_exception`.
+  (NOTE: rank 0 may still block briefly in `dist.destroy_process_group()` NCCL
+  teardown while peers are alive, but the traceback is already printed by then —
+  the launcher/scancel tears the rest down. Diagnosis is no longer blind.)
+- `main.py::_compile_warmup` — wraps the warmup fwd/bwd in try/except that logs
+  the full per-rank traceback before re-raising (this is what unmasked the OOM).
+- `launch_slurm.py::_training_worker` — now installs a root `logging.basicConfig`
+  (INFO→stderr) so main.py's `logger.info` is CAPTURED under submitit (it wasn't
+  before — you were debugging blind). Also sets `TORCH_NCCL_TRACE_BUFFER_SIZE`
+  + `TORCH_NCCL_DUMP_ON_TIMEOUT` so any genuine future collective timeout dumps a
+  FlightRecorder stack.
+
+## RULED OUT (verified — do not re-chase)
+Everything in the prior version of this doc: fabric/IB/GDR, cold-compile/NFS
+FileLock, NCCL version, cgroup isolation, dist bootstrap, liger install. Also NOW
+ruled out: `optimize_ddp` (True or False both OOM when co-tenant present), the
+compile warmup (OOM reproduces with `compile_warmup_steps 0`), and submitit vs
+torchrun (torchrun only "worked" via clean-GPU-0 luck).
+
+## The compile-warmup / optimize_ddp work (separate, still valid)
+`_compile_warmup` (broadcast rank-0 batch → identical graphs) + `optimize_ddp`
+default True remain correct and useful for the *original* narrower first-step
+graph-desync concern, verified on clean-GPU-0 submitit runs. They are simply not
+this bug's fix. Leave them in.
+

